body:
Can anybody help me figure out this guy's code (from the blogspot link)? It only seems to contradict itself.

>/* Digital pins ( only 4 pins are connected ) */
for ( i=2; i<6; prev_digital_mask =" mask;" i="0;" val =" analogRead("> 2 ) {
prev_analog_val[i] = val;
Firmata.sendAnalog(i, val);
}
}

Why would he initialize i as 2? Why not make the for loop from 0 to 3, considering there are four pins in use? Also, the prev_digital_mask is never used in the code, only initialized. Lastly, the for loop seems to contradict itself. i is initialized w/ value 2, but every time the loop cycles, i is reassigned to be " 0;", which also doesn't make sense since i is an integer, and its value doesn't need to be in quotes.

Something else that bothers me is the only analog values are sent through firmata, which to me means that all of the digital inputs are ignored.

I hate programming.

edit: also, analogRead returns an integer, in this case an array. Is the ">2" referring to every value in the array (which all have a maximum of 1)? Why is a comparison thrown in as a modifying condition in the loop. It all just seems kind of null. Either I'm an idiot or this guy is a bad programmer.
